yes(260,'D','X has 8 electrons and is oxygen, which commonly forms X²⁻. Y has 13 electrons and is aluminium, which commonly forms Y³⁺. Two Y ions give +6 and three X ions give −6, so the neutral formula is Y₂X₃.',[PERIODIC,RX],question='Elements X and Y have electron configurations 1s²2s²2p⁴ and 1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p¹ respectively. What is the formula of the compound they form?',options=['XY','YX','X₂Y₃','Y₂X₃'],audit='Restored superscript electron counts and chemical subscripts; verified electron totals and charge balance.',check='aluminium-oxide')
