yes(262,'B','Atomic number 10 is neon. Its electron arrangement is 2,8, with a filled outer shell, so it is a noble gas. The other numbers identify beryllium, magnesium and silicon.',[PERIODIC],question='Elements P, Q, R and S have atomic numbers 4, 10, 12 and 14 respectively. Which is a noble gas?',options=['P','Q','R','S'],check='neon-electrons')
