yes(264,'C','Copper sulfide ores contain sulfur. During roasting and smelting, sulfur is oxidised and sulfur dioxide enters the process gases. Without effective capture, copper smelting is therefore a significant SO₂ emission source.',['https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2020-11/documents/c12s03.pdf'],question='Sulfur dioxide pollution is particularly associated with which industrial activity?',options=['Extracting aluminium from bauxite','Producing margarine','Smelting copper sulfide ores','Producing chlorine from brine'],audit='Specified sulfide ores to explain the actual emission pathway; avoided claiming every modern smelter has uncontrolled emissions.')
no(265,'Lime has several water-treatment roles including pH/alkalinity adjustment and softening. It can support coagulation and subsequent sedimentation under specified conditions, so B and C are not cleanly distinguished by the bare prompt. Need the original treatment stage/reagent context before making a unique key.',answer='B conventional, context needed')
