yes(267,'B','An amphoteric oxide reacts with both acids and bases. ZnO behaves as a base with acid, forming a zinc salt and water, and reacts with strong alkali to form soluble zincate species. This dual behaviour identifies it as amphoteric.',['https://openstax.org/books/chemistry-2e/pages/18-9-occurrence-preparation-and-compounds-of-oxygen','https://sathee.iitk.ac.in/additional-problems-chapterwise/chemistry/d-and-f-block-elements/d-and-f-block-elements_ques_443/','https://myschool.ng/classroom/chemistry/27571?page=276'],question='ZnO dissolves in sodium hydroxide solution and in mineral acid solution to give soluble products. How is ZnO classified?',options=['An allotropic oxide','An amphoteric oxide','A peroxide','A dioxide'],audit='Matching Myschool27571 restores A allotropic oxide and B amphoteric oxide, not inferred from old answer alone.')
yes(268,'B','A Brønsted–Lowry acid forms its conjugate base by losing one proton, H⁺. For example, NH₄⁺ and NH₃ differ by one proton. Their charges differ by one unit, but they need not have opposite charges.',['https://openstax.org/books/chemistry-2e/pages/14-1-bronsted-lowry-acids-and-bases'],question='An acid and its conjugate base',options=['Can neutralise each other to form a salt','Differ by one proton','Differ only by having opposite charges','Are always neutral substances'],audit='Restored missing and; teaching explanation distinguishes a one-unit charge difference from opposite charges.')
no(269,'Cu²⁺ discharge is the intendedA, but source D says Cu²⁺ andSO²⁻ with missing sulfate subscripts. Full original alternative not independently recovered; retain held rather than invent the incomplete sulfur oxyanion distractor.',answer='A')
yes(270,'C','Each cyanide ligand, CN⁻, contributes −1. With six cyanides and Z in oxidation state +2, the total charge is y = +2 + 6(−1) = −4. The anion is therefore [Z(CN)₆]⁴⁻.',[RX],question='An element Z forms the complex anion [Z(CN)₆] with overall charge y. If Z has oxidation number +2, what is y?',options=['−2','−3','−4','−5'],audit='Restored missing Z after If and made y an explicit signed total charge.',check='cyanide-charge')
no(271,'ReactionI prints Fe+2Ag⁺→Fe²⁺+2Ag⁺, failing charge conservation and leaving silver unchanged. D is intended after restoring elementalAg, but an original corroborating the product was not obtained. Hold rather than publish an invalid reaction or silently change its oxidation state.',answer='D conditional on corrected reactionI')
